+40--100 & 7144 & 0.360776 & 0.160345 & 0.057724 & 0.014431\\\bottomrule
+\end{tabular}\end{table}
+
+Each band selects cells with rate at least 1\% of its own peak and takes the linearly interpolated 95th percentile of their required $G$. This resembles one ingredient of EM-M-02, but does not establish its mission-peak eligibility definition or joint channel coverage. At the hypothetical $G=0.3$~cm$^2$~sr, the 10\% counting-target coverages are 93.55, 92.25, 89.66 and 93.25\% of these respective populations. All four meet the 25\% expected-count target in their selected cells. These are not mission-success percentages.
